  "message": "I reviewed the design against the three findings, and I'm not proposing any diagram change. The caller → Lambda (text-statistics) graph has no architecture defect I can fix. None of the three findings can be closed by editing the canvas: application acceptance evidence, provider-schema validation and the requirements review against the emitted configuration all have to be run against this exact export. Until then all three stay open and unverified. That includes whether the caller's ARN exists, the Sydney region (still a candidate), the 64 KiB / 128 MiB / 10 s / concurrency 1 / 30-day log limits, costs, and cleanup (all of these are open). The next engineering steps are: run `terraform validate` with the pinned AWS provider against the export, then run a functional test, a denial test for an unlisted principal, an oversized-input test and a destroy test. Before we can confirm the region, which country must the synthetic test text and its logs stay in?",
